        "authors": [
            {
                "id": 37089709482,
                "preferredName": "Anna S. Zueva",
                "firstName": "Anna S.",
                "lastName": "Zueva"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "A brief history of digital sandboxes used in Russia for testing solutions in the field of artificial intelligence systems for drones and unmanned vehicles is considered. It is shown that the mechanism of regulatory sandboxes is an effective response to modern challenges of advanced information technology development. The article deals with the experience of developing and implementing legal regulation in the use of unmanned vehicles. The results of experimental testing of the automatic drone control system, as well as an analysis of the capabilities and limitations of artificial intelligence, are presented. The importance of legal regulation of this market segment is shown. The main problems of the regulatory framework in this area, ways to solve them and possible consequences are considered. The article provides an overview of the main directions of development of the domestic system of regulating the use of unmanned aerial systems (UAS) in civil aviation. The key directions of development of the regulatory system in the field of unmanned systems, as well as ways of their further development, are considered. The article analyzes the problems that arise in the decision-making process on the use of an unmanned aircraft (UA) at various stages of the UA life cycle.",
