                "firstName": "Yuri M.",
                "lastName": "Baturin"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The article uses the example of new information technologies to examine examples of writers’ predictions of future technical systems with high accuracy and strikingly precise detail. It is shown that literary descriptions are not always visionary, sometimes they are based on scientific predictions or pseudo-scientific descriptions. Nevertheless, as one delves into literary history, one finds ample evidence of writers’ foresight of future technological development. Although the extension of the findings to other fields of technology remains beyond the scope of this article, there is considerable scope for analysing the mechanism of literary-technical foresight.",
